WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.990
Two lines: one with arrowheads,
one with fins pointing outwards.

2
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.440
Which looks longer?

3
00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:08.430
The bottom one, surely.

4
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:11.130
So grab a ruler and measure them both.

5
00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:12.950
Exactly the same.

6
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.730
Now take the ruler away.

7
00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:18.500
The bottom line still looks
longer, even though you know.

8
00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:22.130
So why can't knowing the
truth change what you see?

9
00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:25.960
In this mission, you'll learn that an
illusion is when what you perceive does

10
00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:28.270
not match the physical stimulus.

11
00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.700
Like a bright white triangle,
where no edges are drawn.

12
00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:36.570
And you'll meet size constancy: why a
friend walking off doesn't seem to shrink,

13
00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:39.530
even as their image in your eye does.

14
00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:43.650
Your mission: work out why the
bottom line still looks longer.
